  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Empowerment Center YEC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YEC and Oxfam will provide bottled water (9 litres of water per individual) to the 18,000 displaced individualsor/and those residing in the temporarily shelters. The distribution will follow blanket coverage, considering thedire conditions for all the residents of Gaza. Oxfam will aim to procure and preposition bottled water stock andtransfer the items through Rafah border in coordination with other UN agencies, this activity will commence oncethe Rafah crossing is opened and when there is safe to do so for the programme teams where YEC will beleading on the distribution. In an event of a ceasefire, and the accessibility of goods in Gaza, YEC will undertakea local procurement and consequently leading on the distribution of bottled water. The stocks will be replenishedon the regular basis to ensure regular provision of the bottled water in parallel with the water trucking and watertanks distributions, to ensurethat the critical water provision is ensured before more sustainable solution isimplemented. Atthe time of writing Rafah border crossing remains closed and there is currently no access ofany humanitarian aid whatsoever into Gaza</narrative>
  </description>
